      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T19:44:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wrote this test in two parts in order to have an instantiated surface with no un-flushed commands before starting to replay recordings. But, should we always a) instantiate a target surface and/or b) flush pending work on a surface behind the scenes before replaying to it?",
      "revId": "b2aba653ad98f39a8a6bd0fa8809054a3f2fddcd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "403e2b59_11667f2e",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/MtlRecordingSurfacesTest.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T22:25:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I decided that we should always instantiate the target surface, and in the test I get around worrying about un-flushed commands by manually playing back the surface\u0027s recorder before playing the detached recorder.",
      "parentUuid": "4a2294f5_c9df030c",
      "revId": "b2aba653ad98f39a8a6bd0fa8809054a3f2fddcd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ceb81773_00a74a8c",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/MtlRecordingSurfacesTest.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T13:47:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general we should not be flushing, unflushed commands of the surface. The reason being those will all flush to the surfaces Recorder which may be on another thread doing other work. There is though a small race condition in terms of instantiation here. If a surface has work recorded on a Recorder and that Recorder is snapped at the same time we try to use the special surface, both the snap and special use may try to instantiate the surface at the same time.",
      "parentUuid": "403e2b59_11667f2e",
      "revId": "b2aba653ad98f39a8a6bd0fa8809054a3f2fddcd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d605cf8e_b6f96a80",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/MtlRecordingSurfacesTest.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T21:54:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m understanding the condition correctly, we can have Thread A which directly draws to a surface and then snaps a recording from the surface\u0027s recorder, and then Thread B which has a recording with a special/proxy surface and replays this recording to the actual surface from Thread A. Do we consider this a valid use of special surfaces? In other words, would it better to assert this doesn\u0027t happen, or protect instantiation with a semaphore?",
      "parentUuid": "ceb81773_00a74a8c",
      "revId": "b2aba653ad98f39a8a6bd0fa8809054a3f2fddcd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
